WEBVTT

00:00.420 --> 00:01.253
Instructor: So next up,

00:01.253 --> 00:03.060
we're going to talk about GitHub Pages.

00:03.060 --> 00:05.760
A pretty fun, fun is the wrong term,

00:05.760 --> 00:08.580
I guess useful feature of GitHub

00:08.580 --> 00:12.000
is that we can actually host webpages

00:12.000 --> 00:15.990
out of GitHub repositories for free, very easily,

00:15.990 --> 00:18.390
with basically a single click of a button.

00:18.390 --> 00:22.410
Once our code is up on GitHub, we can host a website.

00:22.410 --> 00:24.000
Now there are some restrictions.

00:24.000 --> 00:26.130
This is not a full-fledged hosting service,

00:26.130 --> 00:29.460
you can't do anything except static webpages.

00:29.460 --> 00:31.740
So that means no server-side languages

00:31.740 --> 00:33.510
like Python, Ruby, or Node.

00:33.510 --> 00:36.240
You're purely HTML, CSS, and JavaScript,

00:36.240 --> 00:39.450
that's what you're limited to, client-side static pages.

00:39.450 --> 00:42.960
But you can still create really amazing portfolio websites

00:42.960 --> 00:47.960
or documentation websites for your repositories.

00:48.240 --> 00:51.030
You can host, you know, if you build a JavaScript game,

00:51.030 --> 00:53.100
you can use GitHub Pages to host that.

00:53.100 --> 00:55.080
But you don't want to use GitHub Pages

00:55.080 --> 00:57.780
for any like high-capacity website

00:57.780 --> 00:59.700
where you're expecting a lot of traffic,

00:59.700 --> 01:01.950
it's not really meant for that.

01:01.950 --> 01:04.140
But it's a really nice feature,

01:04.140 --> 01:07.170
and again, it's free and it's built into GitHub,

01:07.170 --> 01:11.460
so it makes hosting very, very easy for certain situations.

01:11.460 --> 01:12.960
So I'm going to show you some examples.

01:12.960 --> 01:15.270
Here's the GitHub Pages homepage

01:15.270 --> 01:16.500
where they explain how it works,

01:16.500 --> 01:17.880
there's a video you can watch,

01:17.880 --> 01:20.130
then they have the instructions.

01:20.130 --> 01:23.790
But if we go to a project like Faker,

01:23.790 --> 01:26.190
which is a JavaScript library,

01:26.190 --> 01:30.840
this is the actual project on GitHub, it's open-source.

01:30.840 --> 01:33.090
This is the entire repository,

01:33.090 --> 01:36.600
all the collaborators, or contributors, rather.

01:36.600 --> 01:38.490
If I scroll down, though,

01:38.490 --> 01:42.423
there's a link right here to view the documentation.

01:43.290 --> 01:45.030
So it's not the most beautiful website

01:45.030 --> 01:47.040
but it is documentation

01:47.040 --> 01:49.530
and has to do with the library Faker,

01:49.530 --> 01:51.570
it's okay if you have no idea what it is,

01:51.570 --> 01:54.090
but this is docs for this project.

01:54.090 --> 01:55.950
And if you notice this URL,

01:55.950 --> 01:59.670
it has GitHub in the URL, github.io.

01:59.670 --> 02:03.990
So all GitHub pages are going to use that domain github.io.

02:03.990 --> 02:05.790
You can change that, you can actually customize it

02:05.790 --> 02:08.430
and set it up to use your own URL,

02:08.430 --> 02:10.140
but I'm not going to go into that.

02:10.140 --> 02:12.210
But that tells us this is actually hosted

02:12.210 --> 02:14.130
thanks to GitHub Pages.

02:14.130 --> 02:15.840
And here's another example.

02:15.840 --> 02:18.780
This is a repository, oh, I'm on the wrong page.

02:18.780 --> 02:19.860
Here we are.

02:19.860 --> 02:24.030
This repository is a fork of that 2048 game

02:24.030 --> 02:26.800
where somebody, this person here, Ovolve,

02:28.080 --> 02:33.080
Ovolve created an AI solver for the popular game 2048.

02:34.440 --> 02:36.570
So we can see the code here,

02:36.570 --> 02:39.266
but also, thanks to GitHub Pages,

02:39.266 --> 02:42.330
there's this URL I can go to to view the website.

02:42.330 --> 02:43.710
And I don't know if you can see this,

02:43.710 --> 02:48.710
I'll zoom in, hopefully, it's ovolve.github.io/2048-AI.

02:50.520 --> 02:53.400
So it has GitHub in there again, github.io.

02:53.400 --> 02:54.930
So this is another example,

02:54.930 --> 02:57.690
where there's the actual repository,

02:57.690 --> 03:00.930
there's a read me, there's information about the project,

03:00.930 --> 03:03.450
but then, there's a corresponding website

03:03.450 --> 03:05.790
and it happens to be hosted by GitHub.

03:05.790 --> 03:07.470
Same thing that we saw with Faker.

03:07.470 --> 03:10.710
Here is the project, the repository on GitHub.

03:10.710 --> 03:14.310
And here's a website that goes along with that project,

03:14.310 --> 03:16.050
it pertains to that project,

03:16.050 --> 03:19.140
and it has GitHub in that URL as well.

03:19.140 --> 03:22.560
So there are two types, two flavors of GitHub pages.

03:22.560 --> 03:26.220
There are user sites and project sites.

03:26.220 --> 03:28.560
So I'm going to focus on project sites.

03:28.560 --> 03:31.410
For every single GitHub repository you create,

03:31.410 --> 03:34.020
you can have a corresponding hosted website.

03:34.020 --> 03:37.830
So that is, yeah, every single repo you make, every project,

03:37.830 --> 03:40.440
you can have your own corresponding website

03:40.440 --> 03:43.080
and the default URLs are going to follow this pattern.

03:43.080 --> 03:46.320
Whatever your username is, so I'm Colt, is my username,

03:46.320 --> 03:51.090
colt.github.io, slash, and then whatever my repo name is,

03:51.090 --> 03:54.990
you know, portfolio or 2048 clone or something like that.

03:54.990 --> 03:56.610
So that's one per project.

03:56.610 --> 03:59.880
Then there's also user sites.

03:59.880 --> 04:02.910
You are limited to one of those, one per GitHub account.

04:02.910 --> 04:05.850
And this is a different application,

04:05.850 --> 04:07.890
it's actually set up differently as well,

04:07.890 --> 04:09.690
I'm not going to spend as much time on it.

04:09.690 --> 04:11.220
But this is where you could host something

04:11.220 --> 04:14.130
like a personal website, a portfolio,

04:14.130 --> 04:16.140
anything that you want to be based

04:16.140 --> 04:19.290
upon your username.github.io.

04:19.290 --> 04:24.290
So colt.github.io, samanthajones.github.io,

04:24.360 --> 04:27.480
where it's not a project, it's not a particular repository.

04:27.480 --> 04:31.920
Instead, it's about you or your group, your organization,

04:31.920 --> 04:34.860
you are allowed one per GitHub account.

04:34.860 --> 04:37.050
But we're going to focus on project sites

04:37.050 --> 04:38.760
like the two that I showed you.

04:38.760 --> 04:39.960
We have a repo here

04:39.960 --> 04:42.420
and then a corresponding documentation website.

04:42.420 --> 04:43.920
And then we have another repo here,

04:43.920 --> 04:47.700
and then just a deployed version of this project

04:47.700 --> 04:49.020
that we can interact with.

04:49.020 --> 04:50.040
So in the next video,

04:50.040 --> 04:53.100
I'm going to show you how to set this up, it is very simple.

04:53.100 --> 04:56.010
Now you will need to know a little bit of HTML,

04:56.010 --> 04:59.310
just to make websites, but the actual mechanism

04:59.310 --> 05:02.340
to turn it on with GitHub Pages is very easy.

05:02.340 --> 05:03.340
So that's coming up.
